            <div xml:id="d790">

                <pb facs="1043" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6731/163</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 237</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-09">May 9, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received June 28.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It may interest the Department to glance
                    through the exchange of memoranda between the Counselor of the Embassy, who is
                    at the moment in Ankara, and myself, in regard to Turco-American commercial
                    relations.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert P. Skinner</hi></signed></closer>




